ation systems\" for the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(A)\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"indent-3\" id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(A)\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paragraph-hierarchy\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eA\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Magnetic sensors specified by 6A006.a.2 and using optically pumped or nuclear precession (proton/Overhauser) \"technology\" that will permit these sensors to realize a ‘ sensitivity’ lower (better) than 2 pT rms per square root Hz.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(B)\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"indent-3\" id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(B)\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paragraph-hierarchy\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eB\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Underwater electric field sensors specified by 6A006.b.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(C)\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"indent-3\" id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxiv)(C)\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paragraph-hierarchy\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eC\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e \u003cem class=\"paragraph-heading\"\u003e\"Magnetic gradiometers\"\u003c/em\u003e  specified by 6A006.c. that will permit these sensors to realize a ‘ sensitivity’ lower (better) than 3 pT/m rms per square root Hz.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxv)\"\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"indent-2\" id=\"p-Supplement-No.-6-to-Part-774(6)(xxv)\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paragraph-hierarchy\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003exxv\u003cspan class=\"paren\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e 6A006.e—Underwater electromagnetic receivers incorporating \"magnetometers\" sp